  "computation": {
    "horizontal": "x(s) and y(s) are the closed-form integrals of cos(heading) and sin(heading) over lines and circular arcs; heading is the sum of the signed arc angles. Checked against composite 8-point Gauss-Legendre integration with 10 m intervals (agreement better than 1e-9 m). Nothing uses IfcOpenShell geometry.",
    "vertical": "The vertical layout is a single constant 0 % gradient, so z(s) = 0 everywhere.",
    "bbox": "A constant-width band swept along the alignment has its extreme plan coordinates on one of its two edge curves. Both edges are sampled every 0.2 m (including the end), which is well inside the 0.02 m tolerance.",
    "volume": "Cross-section area times horizontal length: the road is flat, so there is no grade correction. The authored IfcSectionedSolidHorizontal has a section every 20 m; the resulting chord approximation differs from the ideal arc volume by less than 0.01 m3.",
    "sectioning": "One IfcSectionedSolidHorizontal per element, directrix = the horizontal IfcCompositeCurve, rectangle profile, cross-section positions every 20 m with OffsetVertical 0."
  },
